 The baseline is exact Git commit 7a90f7934b7c9d1af5c4494bf08c4ec337c373e4 (old D runtime, D2 tests-only change). Authored is the real dispatched `github.sha`, never an invented metadata revision. Each build receives its own actual checked-out SHA through GITHUB_SHA. The original baseline dictionary has 156 entries; authored has 190. Their historical build-info files have revision null. The runner compares the complete asset dictionaries and requires the new build-info revision to match each actual HEAD; it does not pretend the newly committed build-info byte hash equals a historical null-revision hash.
 
